      "objective": "Publish app.preview.test. as 192.0.2.42 and 2001:db8::42. Repair the portal.preview.test. CNAME path to app.preview.test., keeping the portal as an alias. Add mail.preview.test. at 192.0.2.25 and MX preference 10 for the zone. Preserve its nameserver, then bring the secondary to the same current copy.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 20,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the served records and repair the saved zone."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "A/AAAA records hold addresses; CNAME redirects a name; MX identifies a mail host with its own address. Saving and publishing are different. The secondary needs a newer serial to accept the changed primary copy.",
      "hints": [
        "Look up portal A on the primary to see the alias failure.",
        "Add the mail host address as well as the MX record.",
        "After saving, reload the primary and then update the secondary with a newer serial."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1034",
        "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc1982"
